# TEG multi-rect blocks beside a REAL hierarchy — the honest hybrid.
#
# WHY A HYBRID: a BDB component holds ONE bbox, so multi-rect cannot be
# DECLARED as a hier-design input — derive_busterms writes empty rects and
# every BDB->Floorplan projection is add_block(bbox) (see
# docs/internal/teg_multirect_status.md item 6 "RESOLVED-AS-BOUNDED" and
# docs/BDB_REFERENCE.md).  And the two bundlers cannot compose in one
# session either: run_bundler and run_hier_bundler each rebuild
# session.bundles, so the second clobbers the first.  The supported shape
# is therefore HIERARCHY-FED FLAT: build the hierarchy in the BDB, project
# it into the flat floorplan with add_blocks_from_bdb (containers stay
# transparent envelopes, leaves are the routing targets), hand-declare the
# multi-rect TEG macros beside the projection, and route everything with
# the flat pipeline.
#
# What to look at in the viewer:
#   * dsp — an L-shaped teg_mode OVER macro (arm right, base bottom).  The
#     pinned TRUNK_V@x760 drops into the notch and crosses the base only,
#     so BUDA emits a REAL horizontal connector leg from the trunk to the
#     arm (ordinary routed, audited, WL-counted metal — click bundle d).
#   * phy — a disjoint 2-rect OVER block (two slabs, gap between).  The
#     pinned TRUNK_H@y630 runs through the gap and BOTH rects get gap
#     stubs joined through the trunk (click bundle p).
#   * ioc — a 2-rect THRU block: the trunk reaches the near rect only and
#     the far rect is deliberately left to the block's internal routing —
#     the BUDA-1907 census INFO names the untouched rect (report only;
#     thru DECLARES the rects internally connected).
#
# The pins are TYPE specs (select_topology <bus> TRUNK_V@x760), the pin
# that survives a regenerated / re-sorted candidate pool — a hard index
# would not.  Endpoint: 7 bus segments, 28 bit-wires, check_design
# Success at nuts AND dnuts, 0 unplaced.

# ── BDB: a small 2-level hierarchy (2 clusters x 2 PEs) ───────────────
open_bdb :memory:

add_cell cluster 300 280
add_cell pe 110 100
add_inst_to_cell cluster pe0 pe 25 30
add_inst_to_cell cluster pe1 pe 165 150

add_inst cl_bot cluster - 40 40
add_inst cl_top cluster - 40 380

# Project into the flat floorplan: depth 0 = the cluster envelopes
# (auto-marked container once their children load), depth 1 = the PE
# leaves the buses actually target.
add_blocks_from_bdb 0
add_blocks_from_bdb 1 skip

# ── Flat multi-rect TEG macros beside the projected hierarchy ─────────
# dsp: rectilinear L, OVER — rects NOT internally connected, so a trunk
#      that misses the arm owes it explicit connection metal.
add_block dsp rect 900 60 1000 460 rect 620 60 1000 160 teg_mode over
# phy: two disjoint slabs with a horizontal gap (y 580..660), OVER.
add_block phy rect 640 480 1000 580 rect 640 660 1000 760 teg_mode over
# ioc: two disjoint rects, default THRU — internal connectivity declared,
#      so the untouched rect is a census INFO, never a violation.
add_block ioc rect 430 60 540 200 rect 430 300 540 440

def_layer 4 M4 H TOP 50
def_layer 5 M5 V TOP 50

# ── Flat buses: hierarchy leaves -> TEG macros ────────────────────────
add_bus d[4] cl_bot/pe1.out dsp.in
add_bus p[4] cl_top/pe1.out phy.in
add_bus i[4] cl_bot/pe0.out ioc.in

run_bundler STRICT
generate_topologies

def_track_pattern 4 0 (SIGNAL 2 2)x8
def_track_pattern 5 0 (SIGNAL 2 2)x8

# Pin the shapes that SHOW the TEG mechanisms (type specs, 1-based-free):
select_topology d TRUNK_V@x760   # notch trunk -> connector leg to the arm
select_topology p TRUNK_H@y630   # gap trunk   -> per-rect gap stubs
select_topology i TRUNK_H@y120   # near-rect only -> BUDA-1907 census fires

run_planner
run_nuts
check_design
run_detailed_nuts
check_design
report_wl

visualize
